all-state upstream PR title/body searches for `KE-04`, `KE04`, and `block Lanczos`.
Those searches returned the historical Colbrook mathematical submission #6 and
an unrelated KE-05 mathematical submission #143. No competing formalization was
found in that scope. Private, deleted or unidentifiably named work is not covered;
neither the coordinator source note nor the current campaign entry constitutes
an eligibility or statement approval.

The successful author-development attempt is
`verification/statement-development/attempt-r5fn2nl_/result.json`. Its immutable
input copies, exact commands, log hashes, dependency pins before and after,
actual types, definition axiom output and hashes of the removed private objects
are retained. All four modules exited zero: Definitions, Challenge, definition
inspector and type inspector. There are 24 intentional Challenge holes and 27
definition trust assertions. The first attempt's reporting failure is retained;
it expected a success message from a command that succeeds silently, although
its four Lean commands also exited zero. Source-capture failures are also retained.
An initial integrity runner later overwrote the preceding successful attempt's
final JSON through a reused output-path variable. Its immutable source inputs and
Lean logs remain; the lost JSON is not claimed as retained. The misdirected report
and exact diagnosis are in `verification/EVIDENCE-RECOVERY.md` and the referenced
paths. The final attempt named above is a new identical-source run with intact
result, dependency and object-hash records.

This is macOS development elaboration using existing read-only pinned dependency
objects. It is not a full dependency rebuild, proof build, Comparator execution,
raw-kernel export replay or non-root Linux sandbox run. `comparator.json` reserves
all 24 targets, has no replaceable definitions, and allows only the three
foundational axioms; no Solution exists to compare yet.

The package has no independent KE-04 statement approvals and is not frozen.
The statement author and coordinator design feedback do not count as independent
